From ua7af03e957d7de31 at groups.google.com  Mon Apr 24 19:39:07 2017
From: ua7af03e957d7de31 at groups.google.com (Duncan Garmonsway)
Date: Mon, 24 Apr 2017 19:39:07 +0000
Subject: Use get_*() inside log_()
Message-ID: <_wDj1IUvD7c.n3ayYMBVBQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/simmer-devel/c/_wDj1IUvD7c/m/n3ayYMBVBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

Is it possible to use the `get_*()` functions inside `log_()`?  This is possible for decision-making, e.g. branching, but inside `log_()` I'm having trouble with mutual dependencies, nomatter whether the trajectory or the simulation environment is defined first.

``` r
library(simmer)

customer <- trajectory() %>%
  log_(get_queue_count(bank, "counter"))
#> Warning in value[[3L]](cond): restarting interrupted promise evaluation

#> Warning in value[[3L]](cond): restarting interrupted promise evaluation

#> Warning in value[[3L]](cond): restarting interrupted promise evaluation
#> Error in get_queue_count(bank, "counter"): object 'bank' not found

bank <- simmer() %>%
  add_resource("counter") %>%
  add_generator("Customer", customer, at(0))
#> Error in inherits(trajectory, "trajectory"): object 'customer' not found
```

Thanks,
Duncan

From u0f5b7adb7e70bd8b at groups.google.com  Mon Apr 24 19:48:37 2017
From: u0f5b7adb7e70bd8b at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?b?ScOxYWtpIMOaY2Fy?=)
Date: Mon, 24 Apr 2017 19:48:37 +0000
Subject: Re: [simmer-devel] Use get_*() inside log_()
Message-ID: <_wDj1IUvD7c.kmWL9ERWBQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <_wDj1IUvD7c.n3ayYMBVBQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
References: <_wDj1IUvD7c.n3ayYMBVBQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/simmer-devel/c/_wDj1IUvD7c/m/kmWL9ERWBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Yes, it is, but as in branching, you need to enclose them inside a function:

> log_(function() paste(get_queue_count(bank, "counter")))

Iñaki

